WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.823 --> 00:00:17.045
Mowgli could smell things better than most humans could.

2
00:00:17.705 --> 00:00:20.027
But he did not have a true jungle nose.

3
00:00:20.947 --> 00:00:23.148
So it took him longer to find the scent.

4
00:00:27.111 --> 00:00:28.251
"It's Buldeo!"

5
00:00:28.571 --> 00:00:29.212
he whispered.

6
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.821
"He must have followed my trail.

7
00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:35.282
I can see the sunlight glinting off his gun.

8
00:00:35.903 --> 00:00:40.465
Look!" There was just a quick flash of light among some shrubs.

9
00:00:41.085 --> 00:00:42.265
But they all saw it.

10
00:00:43.346 --> 00:00:46.127
The four young wolves suddenly ran downhill.

11
00:00:46.147 --> 00:00:48.528
"Where are you going?"

12
00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:49.609
Mowgli said.

13
00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:53.290
"Hunting!" Gray Brother answered.

14
00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.931
"Come on with us!"

15
00:00:54.951 --> 00:00:57.172
"I can't.

16
00:00:57.768 --> 00:01:00.169
Humans do not hunt other humans!"

17
00:01:00.909 --> 00:01:02.190
Mowgli called after them.

18
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:06.152
Akela gazed at him, and Mowgli looked away.

19
00:01:06.172 --> 00:01:11.354
"Let's just find this man and see what he wants," Bagheera said.

20
00:01:13.435 --> 00:01:18.477
Mowgli ran forward, darting noiselessly through the jungle behind the young wolves.

21
00:01:20.918 --> 00:01:21.918
The others followed.

22
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.475
Sure enough, when Mowgli pushed aside some bushes, there was Buldeo.

23
00:01:31.536 --> 00:01:35.098
His gun on one shoulder, the hunter trotted along the path.

24
00:01:36.199 --> 00:01:39.661
Abruptly he halted, looking at the ground in confusion.

25
00:01:40.982 --> 00:01:43.764
Akela chuckled softly from beside Mowgli.

26
00:01:43.784 --> 00:01:48.267
"This morning I added some prints to the trail.

27
00:01:49.188 --> 00:01:51.449
They're going in all different directions."

28
00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:57.430
"No wonder Buldeo is confused," Mowgli whispered with a grin.

29
00:01:58.691 --> 00:02:01.673
Finally the hunter grunted and sat down.

30
00:02:02.594 --> 00:02:07.619
He had no idea that Mowgli and the animals were nearby, watching him.

31
00:02:08.599 --> 00:02:10.441
He muttered angrily to himself.

32
00:02:11.922 --> 00:02:12.823
"What is he saying?"

33
00:02:13.243 --> 00:02:14.705
Bagheera asked Mowgli.

34
00:02:15.926 --> 00:02:18.228
He quickly translated Buldeo's words.

35
00:02:18.248 --> 00:02:22.772
"He says, 'packs of wolves must have danced round me.

36
00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.681
I never saw a trail like this!'

37
00:02:27.621 --> 00:02:30.682
Now he's complaining about being tired and hungry."

38
00:02:31.823 --> 00:02:33.303
Buldeo ate some nuts.

39
00:02:35.224 --> 00:02:37.964
Soon some other men wandered along the trail.

40
00:02:38.965 --> 00:02:40.805
They sat down for a rest too.

41
00:02:41.906 --> 00:02:45.027
Buldeo began telling them some wild stories.

42
00:02:46.847 --> 00:02:49.308
Mowgli nearly laughed aloud as he listened.

43
00:02:50.392 --> 00:02:54.775
Buldeo was telling the men that he had killed the great tiger, Shere Khan.

44
00:02:55.476 --> 00:02:58.958
Then he said that a boy had turned himself into a wolf.

45
00:03:00.259 --> 00:03:03.601
"I fought with him all afternoon," the hunter said.

46
00:03:03.621 --> 00:03:06.943
"I think he used magic on my gun."

47
00:03:06.963 --> 00:03:09.685
"What makes you say that?"

48
00:03:10.146 --> 00:03:11.206
one of the men asked.

49
00:03:11.226 --> 00:03:15.890
"A bullet meant for him suddenly spun around.

50
00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:19.152
It went into one of my own buffalo!

51
00:03:20.128 --> 00:03:21.209
I'm the chief hunter.

52
00:03:21.609 --> 00:03:23.970
So my village has sent me to hunt him down."

53
00:03:25.411 --> 00:03:27.913
Mowgli's friends glanced over, worried.

54
00:03:28.653 --> 00:03:31.035
However, Mowgli was still grinning.

55
00:03:31.055 --> 00:03:33.736
"His stories are ridiculous.

56
00:03:34.637 --> 00:03:36.438
But the other men believe him!"

57
00:03:36.458 --> 00:03:43.122
"Meanwhile the villagers have locked up Messua and her husband," Buldeo was saying.

58
00:03:43.142 --> 00:03:45.623
"They are sorcerers too.

59
00:03:46.464 --> 00:03:51.111
In fact, they are the worst kind because they were raising this wolf child.

60
00:03:51.912 --> 00:03:55.515
They will be punished—perhaps even burned to death."

61
00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:58.757
The men gasped.

62
00:03:59.518 --> 00:04:01.019
"When?" one asked.

63
00:04:01.039 --> 00:04:07.664
"Nothing will be done until I return with the boy's dead body," Buldeo replied.

64
00:04:07.685 --> 00:04:11.668
"By the way, I have reason to think he's nearby.

65
00:04:12.388 --> 00:04:13.089
Have you seen him?"

66
00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.672
Bagheera glanced at Mowgli again.

67
00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.362
He noticed that the boy's expression had changed.

68
00:04:20.382 --> 00:04:23.084
"What are the men saying?"

69
00:04:23.545 --> 00:04:24.586
the panther whispered.

70
00:04:25.566 --> 00:04:28.329
With a grim look, Mowgli translated.

71
00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.333
He explained the villagers had trapped Messua and her husband.

72
00:04:34.754 --> 00:04:38.657
"What?" Gray Brother shook his head in confusion.

73
00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:41.779
"Humans trap each other?"

74
00:04:41.799 --> 00:04:45.362
"So Buldeo says."

75
00:04:46.003 --> 00:04:47.124
Mowgli scowled.

76
00:04:47.996 --> 00:04:52.158
"I cannot understand all his talk—people are crazy.

77
00:04:53.558 --> 00:04:58.821
But I do know this: Messua and her husband have done nothing wrong.

78
00:04:59.741 --> 00:05:02.382
All they did was feed me and shelter me."

79
00:05:03.743 --> 00:05:05.904
Mowgli listened to Buldeo some more.

80
00:05:07.064 --> 00:05:09.865
His expression grew more and more determined.

81
00:05:09.885 --> 00:05:12.827
"I am going back to the village.

82
00:05:13.807 --> 00:05:14.988
I won't let them kill
